(2375, 6, '2017-10-26 12:57:42', '2017-10-26 12:57:42', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2224\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 50px\">About Us</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<div id=\"what-we-do\" class=\"section--header\">\r\n<h2 class=\"section--title\" style=\"text-align: center\">What is BIR ?</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;margin: 0 0 13px;text-align: center\">Who we are</h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">Ondo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic ocean.\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.\r\nThe board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex government agency charge with the responsibility of superintending internally generated revenue (IGR) in Ondo state. It is a creation of the Personal Income Tax Act 2004(as amended). Its statutory responsibilities are contained in Section 88 subsection listed below.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Ensuring the effectiveness and optimum collection of all taxes and penalties due to the government under the relevant laws.</li>\r\n 	<li>Doing all such things as may be deemed necessary and expedient for the assessment and collection of taxes and shall account for all amounts so collected in a manner to be prescribed by the Commissioner.</li>\r\n 	<li>Appointing, promoting, transferring and imposing discipline on employees of the state service.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Making recommendations where appropriate to the Joint Tax Board (JTB) on tax policy; tax reform; tax legislation: tax treaties and exception as m,ay be required, from time to time.</li>\r\n 	<li>Generally controlling the management of the State service on matter of policy subject to the provisions of the laws setting up the state service, and;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"section--overlap\"][vc_column width=\"6/12\" css=\".vc_custom_1470146937754{padding-top: 200px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">What BIR</h3>\r\nOndo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][pillar_team][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column width=\"5/12\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3>\"Your Child, Our Future\". Innovation through education.</h3>\r\nPillar is a remarkably flexible and feature-complete HTML template built for modern startups, creatives, bloggers and more. Including tons of uniquely styled pages, Pillar combines aesthetic beauty with high-quality, semantic markup.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/12\"][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"6/12\"][pillar_video_inline image=\"1197\" webm=\"http://pillar.tommusdemos.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/43/2016/06/video.webm\" mpfour=\"http://pillar.tommusdemos.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/43/2016/06/video.mp4\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Subscribe for updates and events</h4>\r\n<p class=\"lead\" style=\"text-align: center\">Stay in the loop with our monthly round-up of important news updates.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][contact-form-7 id=\"344\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1470147553763{padding-top: 80px !important;padding-bottom: 60px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Interested in contributing to the cause?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">DONATE TODAY</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'About Us', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '271-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-26 12:57:42', '2017-10-26 12:57:42', '', 271, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/26/271-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2378, 6, '2017-10-26 13:18:40', '2017-10-26 13:18:40', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2224\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 50px\">About Us</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<div id=\"what-we-do\" style=\"font-size: 20px;line-height: 30px;color: #9b9b9b;text-align: center;margin: 13px 0 0\">\r\n<h2 class=\"section--title\" style=\"text-align: center\">Everything About BIR</h2>\r\nWe are a tax collecting Agency\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;margin: 0 0 13px;text-align: center\">Who we are</h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">Ondo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic ocean.\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.\r\nThe board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex government agency charge with the responsibility of superintending internally generated revenue (IGR) in Ondo state. It is a creation of the Personal Income Tax Act 2004(as amended). Its statutory responsibilities are contained in Section 88 subsection listed below.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Ensuring the effectiveness and optimum collection of all taxes and penalties due to the government under the relevant laws.</li>\r\n 	<li>Doing all such things as may be deemed necessary and expedient for the assessment and collection of taxes and shall account for all amounts so collected in a manner to be prescribed by the Commissioner.</li>\r\n 	<li>Appointing, promoting, transferring and imposing discipline on employees of the state service.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Making recommendations where appropriate to the Joint Tax Board (JTB) on tax policy; tax reform; tax legislation: tax treaties and exception as m,ay be required, from time to time.</li>\r\n 	<li>Generally controlling the management of the State service on matter of policy subject to the provisions of the laws setting up the state service, and;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">Mission &amp; Vision</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"section--overlap\"][vc_column width=\"6/12\" css=\".vc_custom_1470146937754{padding-top: 200px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">What BIR</h3>\r\nOndo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][pillar_team][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Subscribe for updates and events</h4>\r\n<p class=\"lead\" style=\"text-align: center\">Stay in the loop with our monthly round-up of important news updates.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][contact-form-7 id=\"344\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1470147553763{padding-top: 80px !important;padding-bottom: 60px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Interested in contributing to the cause?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">DONATE TODAY</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'About Us', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '271-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-26 13:18:40', '2017-10-26 13:18:40', '', 271, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/26/271-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2380, 6, '2017-10-26 13:39:57', '2017-10-26 13:39:57', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2224\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 50px\">About Us</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<div id=\"what-we-do\" style=\"font-size: 20px;line-height: 30px;color: #9b9b9b;text-align: center;margin: 13px 0 0\">\r\n<h2 class=\"section--title\" style=\"text-align: center\">Everything About BIR</h2>\r\nWe are a tax collecting Agency\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;margin: 0 0 13px;text-align: center\">Who we are</h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">Ondo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic ocean.\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.\r\nThe board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex government agency charge with the responsibility of superintending internally generated revenue (IGR) in Ondo state. It is a creation of the Personal Income Tax Act 2004(as amended). Its statutory responsibilities are contained in Section 88 subsection listed below.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Ensuring the effectiveness and optimum collection of all taxes and penalties due to the government under the relevant laws.</li>\r\n 	<li>Doing all such things as may be deemed necessary and expedient for the assessment and collection of taxes and shall account for all amounts so collected in a manner to be prescribed by the Commissioner.</li>\r\n 	<li>Appointing, promoting, transferring and imposing discipline on employees of the state service.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Making recommendations where appropriate to the Joint Tax Board (JTB) on tax policy; tax reform; tax legislation: tax treaties and exception as m,ay be required, from time to time.</li>\r\n 	<li>Generally controlling the management of the State service on matter of policy subject to the provisions of the laws setting up the state service, and;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_icon type=\"typicons\" icon_typicons=\"typcn typcn-flag-outline\" color=\"orange\" background_style=\"rounded\" align=\"center\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">Mission</h3>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px;text-align: center\">To achieve sustainable annual incremental growth of Internally Generated Revenue(IGR)</p>\r\n\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">Vision</h3>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px;text-align: center\">Widening and deepening internally generated revenue to adequately fund recurrent expenditure and Institutionalizing a robust and effective payment platform capable of propelling internally generated revenue into a pivot for public finance</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 20px;font-weight: 300\">Our Management Team</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][pillar_team][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Subscribe for updates and events</h4>\r\n<p class=\"lead\" style=\"text-align: center\">Stay in the loop with our monthly round-up of important news updates.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][contact-form-7 id=\"344\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1470147553763{padding-top: 80px !important;padding-bottom: 60px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Interested in contributing to the cause?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">DONATE TODAY</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'About Us', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '271-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-26 13:39:57', '2017-10-26 13:39:57', '', 271, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/26/271-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2379, 6, '2017-10-26 13:23:05', '2017-10-26 13:23:05', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2224\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 50px\">About Us</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<div id=\"what-we-do\" style=\"font-size: 20px;line-height: 30px;color: #9b9b9b;text-align: center;margin: 13px 0 0\">\r\n<h2 class=\"section--title\" style=\"text-align: center\">Everything About BIR</h2>\r\nWe are a tax collecting Agency\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;margin: 0 0 13px;text-align: center\">Who we are</h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">Ondo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic ocean.\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.\r\nThe board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex government agency charge with the responsibility of superintending internally generated revenue (IGR) in Ondo state. It is a creation of the Personal Income Tax Act 2004(as amended). Its statutory responsibilities are contained in Section 88 subsection listed below.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Ensuring the effectiveness and optimum collection of all taxes and penalties due to the government under the relevant laws.</li>\r\n 	<li>Doing all such things as may be deemed necessary and expedient for the assessment and collection of taxes and shall account for all amounts so collected in a manner to be prescribed by the Commissioner.</li>\r\n 	<li>Appointing, promoting, transferring and imposing discipline on employees of the state service.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<ul style=\"font-size: 16px\">\r\n 	<li>Making recommendations where appropriate to the Joint Tax Board (JTB) on tax policy; tax reform; tax legislation: tax treaties and exception as m,ay be required, from time to time.</li>\r\n 	<li>Generally controlling the management of the State service on matter of policy subject to the provisions of the laws setting up the state service, and;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">Mission &amp; Vision</h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">To achieve sustainable annual incremental growth of Internally Generated Revenue(IGR)</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;font-size: 16px\">Widening and deepening internally generated revenue to adequately fund recurrent expenditure\r\nInstitutionalizing a robust and effective payment platform capable of propelling internally generated revenue into a pivot for public finance</p>\r\n [/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"section--overlap\"][vc_column width=\"6/12\" css=\".vc_custom_1470146937754{padding-top: 200px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center\">What BIR</h3>\r\nOndo state is located in the tropical forest of South western part of Nigeria, bounded in the north by Ekiti and Kogi states, in the east by Edo state, in the west by Osun and Ogun states and in the south by the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nThe states which has a fairly considerable population(put at about 3.44 million in 2006) possesses what it takes to be a haven of rewarding commercial activities and an economy backbone of the nation. Ondo state is richly blessed with copious natural resources waiting to be tapped. The strategic location of the state coupled with its peaceful and safe environment makes it very attractive to investors. Key areas of investment in the state are mineral resources exploration, agriculture and agro processing, tourism and infrastructure.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][pillar_team][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--secondary\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Subscribe for updates and events</h4>\r\n<p class=\"lead\" style=\"text-align: center\">Stay in the loop with our monthly round-up of important news updates.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][contact-form-7 id=\"344\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1470147553763{padding-top: 80px !important;padding-bottom: 60px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center\">Interested in contributing to the cause?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">DONATE TODAY</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'About Us', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '271-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-26 13:23:05', '2017-10-26 13:23:05', '', 271, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/26/271-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
