(2473, 6, '2017-10-30 12:56:07', '2017-10-30 12:56:07', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2435\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 50px;text-align: left;font-weight: 400;margin-bottom: 2px\">Tax Types</h3>\r\nThe different tax types used by the ondo BIR[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509113664080{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">STAMP DUTIES TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Stamp Duties Tax is backed by the Stamp Duties Act, Cap. 441 LFN, 1990. The tax provides for the levying of stamp duties on certain matters. The power to collect Stamp Duties by the State Tax Authority is enshrined in Section 4(2) where the State is given the power to collect the duties in respect of instruments executed between persons or individuals at such rates to be imposed or charged as may be agreed with the Federal Government.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">3% of the consideration in the Document i.e amount stated in the document</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">However, re-assessment may be done taking into consideration the current market value of the property. (make room for Best of Judgement BOJ)</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116029069{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CONSUMPTION TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">This Tax is backed by the “Hotels and Event Centres Occupancy and Restaurant Consumption Law (2011),” and is targeted at the hospitality industry to ensure that patrons of such outfits pay to Government a minimum tax of 5% of the total bill of the item or service consumed at these facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116138384{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PAYE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Pay As You Earn (PAYE) is a provision under the Personal Income Tax Act, 2004 (as amended) and it is the taxation of income of individuals derived from employment. This income includes salaries, wages, bonuses, allowances and benefits in kind.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">WITHHOLDING TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">These are taxes paid on contract awarded by establishments; It can also be defined as a government requirement for the payer of an item of income to withhold or deduct tax from the payment, and pay that tax to the government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"zw-table\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">S/N</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">ITEM</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">PERCENTAGE</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">DEPENDENT</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Interest and Deposit</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Interest</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">3</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Dividend</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Dividend</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Consultancy</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Consultancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Agency and Contract</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Contract</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">6</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Construction</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Construction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">7</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Management Service</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Service</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">8</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Commission</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Commisson</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">9</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Royalty</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Royalty</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Director’s Fee</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Fee</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PERSONAL INCOME TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Personal Income Tax is tax that is levied on the income of individuals who are either in employment or are engaged in their own business. The Tax encompasses both PAYE and Direct Assessment.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CAPITAL GAINS TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Capital Gains Tax is backed by the Capital Gains Tax Act, Cap. 354, LFN 1990. It is the taxation of capital gains accruing on the disposal of assets.10% of the gain from the sales of a fixed asset</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">LAND USE CHARGE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge Tax is backed by The Land Use Charge Law (2012) which was introduced to consolidate all land based charges under one single charge for ease of administration and collection.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge incorporates the Ground Rent which is provided for under the Land Use Act; Tenement Rate which is provided for under the Local Government Law; and the Property Tax which is provided for under the Land Use ChargeLaw. As determined by Ministry of Housing and Ministry of Land and Survey.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">DIRECT ASSESSMENT</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Direct Assessment is an Income Tax which is imposed on self employed persons e.g. Directors, Accountants, Traders, Hair Dressers, Carpenters, Lawyers, Mechanics, Vulcanizers, artisans etc. Download full documentation on Direct Assessment processes here</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Tax Types', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '572-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-30 12:56:07', '2017-10-30 12:56:07', '', 572, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/30/572-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2474, 6, '2017-10-30 13:00:54', '2017-10-30 13:00:54', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2435\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 50px;text-align: left;font-weight: 400;margin-bottom: 2px\">Tax Types</h3>\r\nThe different taxes collected to drive economic\r\ngrowth and development[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509113664080{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">STAMP DUTIES TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Stamp Duties Tax is backed by the Stamp Duties Act, Cap. 441 LFN, 1990. The tax provides for the levying of stamp duties on certain matters. The power to collect Stamp Duties by the State Tax Authority is enshrined in Section 4(2) where the State is given the power to collect the duties in respect of instruments executed between persons or individuals at such rates to be imposed or charged as may be agreed with the Federal Government.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">3% of the consideration in the Document i.e amount stated in the document</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">However, re-assessment may be done taking into consideration the current market value of the property. (make room for Best of Judgement BOJ)</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116029069{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CONSUMPTION TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">This Tax is backed by the “Hotels and Event Centres Occupancy and Restaurant Consumption Law (2011),” and is targeted at the hospitality industry to ensure that patrons of such outfits pay to Government a minimum tax of 5% of the total bill of the item or service consumed at these facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116138384{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PAYE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Pay As You Earn (PAYE) is a provision under the Personal Income Tax Act, 2004 (as amended) and it is the taxation of income of individuals derived from employment. This income includes salaries, wages, bonuses, allowances and benefits in kind.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">WITHHOLDING TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">These are taxes paid on contract awarded by establishments; It can also be defined as a government requirement for the payer of an item of income to withhold or deduct tax from the payment, and pay that tax to the government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"zw-table\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">S/N</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">ITEM</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">PERCENTAGE</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">DEPENDENT</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Interest and Deposit</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Interest</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">3</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Dividend</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Dividend</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Consultancy</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Consultancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Agency and Contract</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Contract</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">6</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Construction</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Construction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">7</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Management Service</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Service</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">8</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Commission</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Commisson</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">9</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Royalty</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Royalty</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Director’s Fee</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Fee</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PERSONAL INCOME TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Personal Income Tax is tax that is levied on the income of individuals who are either in employment or are engaged in their own business. The Tax encompasses both PAYE and Direct Assessment.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CAPITAL GAINS TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Capital Gains Tax is backed by the Capital Gains Tax Act, Cap. 354, LFN 1990. It is the taxation of capital gains accruing on the disposal of assets.10% of the gain from the sales of a fixed asset</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">LAND USE CHARGE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge Tax is backed by The Land Use Charge Law (2012) which was introduced to consolidate all land based charges under one single charge for ease of administration and collection.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge incorporates the Ground Rent which is provided for under the Land Use Act; Tenement Rate which is provided for under the Local Government Law; and the Property Tax which is provided for under the Land Use ChargeLaw. As determined by Ministry of Housing and Ministry of Land and Survey.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">DIRECT ASSESSMENT</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Direct Assessment is an Income Tax which is imposed on self employed persons e.g. Directors, Accountants, Traders, Hair Dressers, Carpenters, Lawyers, Mechanics, Vulcanizers, artisans etc. Download full documentation on Direct Assessment processes here</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Tax Types', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '572-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-30 13:00:54', '2017-10-30 13:00:54', '', 572, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/30/572-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2475, 6, '2017-10-30 13:02:14', '2017-10-30 13:02:14', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2435\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 50px;text-align: left;font-weight: 400;margin-bottom: 2px\">Tax Types</h3>\r\nThe different taxes collected to drive economic\r\ngrowth and development.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509113664080{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">STAMP DUTIES TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Stamp Duties Tax is backed by the Stamp Duties Act, Cap. 441 LFN, 1990. The tax provides for the levying of stamp duties on certain matters. The power to collect Stamp Duties by the State Tax Authority is enshrined in Section 4(2) where the State is given the power to collect the duties in respect of instruments executed between persons or individuals at such rates to be imposed or charged as may be agreed with the Federal Government.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">3% of the consideration in the Document i.e amount stated in the document</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">However, re-assessment may be done taking into consideration the current market value of the property. (make room for Best of Judgement BOJ)</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116029069{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CONSUMPTION TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">This Tax is backed by the “Hotels and Event Centres Occupancy and Restaurant Consumption Law (2011),” and is targeted at the hospitality industry to ensure that patrons of such outfits pay to Government a minimum tax of 5% of the total bill of the item or service consumed at these facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115400307{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116138384{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PAYE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Pay As You Earn (PAYE) is a provision under the Personal Income Tax Act, 2004 (as amended) and it is the taxation of income of individuals derived from employment. This income includes salaries, wages, bonuses, allowances and benefits in kind.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">WITHHOLDING TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">These are taxes paid on contract awarded by establishments; It can also be defined as a government requirement for the payer of an item of income to withhold or deduct tax from the payment, and pay that tax to the government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"zw-table\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">S/N</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">ITEM</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">PERCENTAGE</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">DEPENDENT</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Rent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Interest and Deposit</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Interest</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">3</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Dividend</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Dividend</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Consultancy</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Consultancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Agency and Contract</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Contract</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">6</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Construction</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Construction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">7</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Management Service</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Service</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">8</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Commission</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Commisson</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">9</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Royalty</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">5%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Royalty</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">WHT on Director’s Fee</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">10%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td class=\"zw-td\">\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\">Value of Fee</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\"><span class=\"EOP\"> </span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">PERSONAL INCOME TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Personal Income Tax is tax that is levied on the income of individuals who are either in employment or are engaged in their own business. The Tax encompasses both PAYE and Direct Assessment.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">CAPITAL GAINS TAX</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Capital Gains Tax is backed by the Capital Gains Tax Act, Cap. 354, LFN 1990. It is the taxation of capital gains accruing on the disposal of assets.10% of the gain from the sales of a fixed asset</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">LAND USE CHARGE</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge Tax is backed by The Land Use Charge Law (2012) which was introduced to consolidate all land based charges under one single charge for ease of administration and collection.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">The Land Use Charge incorporates the Ground Rent which is provided for under the Land Use Act; Tenement Rate which is provided for under the Local Government Law; and the Property Tax which is provided for under the Land Use ChargeLaw. As determined by Ministry of Housing and Ministry of Land and Survey.</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][vc_icon icon_fontawesome=\"fa fa-play\" color=\"custom\" size=\"xs\" css=\".vc_custom_1509115419998{margin-right: 0px !important;border-right-width: 0px !important;padding-right: 0px !important;}\" custom_color=\"#f48148\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\" css=\".vc_custom_1509116183629{margin-top: 16px !important;margin-left: -230px !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 26px;font-weight: 400\">DIRECT ASSESSMENT</h2>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px\">Direct Assessment is an Income Tax which is imposed on self employed persons e.g. Directors, Accountants, Traders, Hair Dressers, Carpenters, Lawyers, Mechanics, Vulcanizers, artisans etc. Download full documentation on Direct Assessment processes here</p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Tax Types', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '572-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-30 13:02:14', '2017-10-30 13:02:14', '', 572, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/30/572-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2477, 6, '2017-10-30 13:06:25', '2017-10-30 13:06:25', '[vc_row parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2286\" css=\".vc_custom_1508942512465{padding-top: -50px !important;padding-bottom: 170px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 50px;text-align: left;font-weight: 400;margin-bottom: 2px\">Our Locations</h3>\r\nFind the closest tax office to\r\npay your tax.\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner][pillar_accordion type=\"accordion accordion--oneopen\"][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Akoko North East\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>         CJO/3 Olorunsogo Street, Opposite Oke Royal Hospital,\r\nIdi Mango, Ikare Akoko </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Akoko North-West, Oke Agbe\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>Balogun Compound, Afufu junction, Ikese quarters, Oka Akoko </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Oke AroIsikan, Akure\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>4 Afunbiowo st., Prof. Falaye’s Building, Akure </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Oyemekun, akure\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>Alagbaka quarters, Akure </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Idanre\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\n23, Okebola street, Opposite Afribank, idanre</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ilaje, Igbokoda\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nAdjacent Imisi petrol station, Okiti pupa road, Igbokoda</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Irele, Ode Irele\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nFormer VAT office, ebute road, ode irele</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ore/Lagos, Ore\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBeside Magistrate court, ominla, Old Lagos rd, Ore</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ondo East, Bolorunduro\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nGenral Hospital, Bolorunduro</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Sabo/Ondo, Ondo\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBarracks rd, Along GRA, Ondo\r\n</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ose, Ifon\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nOpposite Rtd. Col. Awodeyi’s house, Sobe rd., Ifon\r\n</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Owo\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nQuarters 10-12 GRA, Ijebu-Owo, Owo</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][/pillar_accordion][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner][pillar_accordion type=\"accordion accordion--oneopen\"][pillar_accordion_content title=\"AkokoSouth-East, Isua\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>10 Ese quarters, Isua, Isua-Akoko </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Akoko North, Iju/Itaogbolu\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>Jegele’s House, beside Alamo Grammer School, junction Itaogbolu </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Akure express/Akure\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>Alagbaka quarters, Akure </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"AkokoSouth-West, Oka\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBalogun Compound, Afufu junction, Ikese quarters, Oka Akoko</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Oba Adesida, Akure\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>JAlagbaka quarters, Akure </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ijoka/Oshinle, Akure\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>Alagbaka quarters, Akure </strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ese Odo, Igbekebo\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBehind Local Govt. Secretariat,Igbekebo</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ifedore, Igbara Oke\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\n1 market road, opposite St. Paul Ang.Church, Igbara oke</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ile Oluji/Okeigbo, Ile-Oluji\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\n36, Ajifererestreet, opposite L.A. Pry School, Ondo rd., Ile Oluji\r\n</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Ore/Benin, Ore\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBeside Magistrate court, ominla, Old Lagos rd, Ore\r\n</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Okitipupa, Okitipupa\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBarracks rd, Along GRA, Ondo\r\n</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Yaba/Ondo, Ondo\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;margin-left: 28px\"><strong>\r\nBarracks rd, Along GRA, Ondo</strong></p>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][/pillar_accordion][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Our Locations', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1325-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-30 13:06:25', '2017-10-30 13:06:25', '', 1325, 'http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/2017/10/30/1325-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
