(3137, 6, '2018-04-12 09:11:41', '2018-04-12 09:11:41', '[vc_row full_height=\"yes\" parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"2348\"][vc_column css=\".vc_custom_1523031624157{background-position: center !important;background-repeat: no-repeat !important;background-size: cover !important;}\"][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">FAQs</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_empty_space height=\"5rem\"][vc_text_separator title=\"Personal Income Tax (PIT)\"][pillar_accordion type=\"accordion accordion--oneopen\"][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What is tax?\"]Tax is a compulsory levy imposed on the citizen and resident of a state by the government to generate the funds needed for her responsibilities.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What is the basis of assessment of a taxpayer to personal income tax (PIT)?\"]A taxpayer is assessed to tax based on his/her aggregate income from all sources.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What incomes are chargeable to tax? \"]The income chargeable to tax are gains/profit from any trade, business, profession, vocation, salary/wages/fee/allowance/benefit-in-kind and other perquisites enjoyed by a taxpayer.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Does payment of tax confer any special benefits(s)? \"]The benefit are directly to the general public and not to any particular individual. However, payment of tax is a perquisite to access some public amenities.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What happens if someone fails to pay tax?\"]It is an offence punishable by law because tax is statutory obligation of an individual the various offences and penalties are as stated in the relevant provision of the personal income tax act (PITA)[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Does a taxpayer have the right to object to an assessment?\"]Yes, the objection which must be in writing, stating the grounds of objection, must be made within 30 days of service of assessment notice.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What are the procedures involved in the payment of tax? \"]\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>Filing of annual returns (income declaration) with the board of internal revenue(BIR)</li>\r\n 	<li>Assessment of taxpayers.</li>\r\n 	<li>Collection of payment advice from board of internal revenue (BIR).</li>\r\n 	<li>Payment of tax into state government account in any of the designated banks.</li>\r\n 	<li>Collection of e-Receipt from the office BIR.</li>\r\n 	<li>Printing of receipt from dedicated portal</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Are there penalties for failure to pay any statutory taxes/levies/rate due to the state government?\"]Yes, a defaulter’s business premises could be sealed, his/her goods/properties/cartels could be impounded and the impounded items sold to defray the tax liabilities.[/pillar_accordion_content][/pillar_accordion][vc_empty_space height=\"5rem\"][vc_text_separator title=\"Religious Organization\"][pillar_accordion type=\"accordion accordion--oneopen\"][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Are religious organisations liable to pay taxes?\"]No. the third schedule (section 19 (1) 74) item 2 to personal income tax act CAP P8 LFN 2004 as amended “exempts the income of any ecclesiastical, charitable or educational institution of a public character from taxation provided the income is not derived from a trade or business carried on by such institution”. The importance of this provision is that incomes of the religious bodies from religious activities e.g. tithe, offerings, donations, are not taxable. The following are however taxable:\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>Income derived from business activities e.g. letting of properties , transportation, production and sales of journals, periodicals, audios&amp;video CDs etc., where these activities are carried out in the name of a separate entity or for profit.</li>\r\n 	<li>Where religious organisations funds are used to acquire assets i.e. motor vehicles, landed property etc.in name different from that of the religious organisation or in the name of an individual who is associated with the religious organisation, funds so expended become income in the hand of the entity/individuals and such are taxable.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"I am a religious leader, should I pay personal income tax on a monthly salary/allowance/financial donations I receive from the religious organisation I work for or from other source?\"]Yes section 24(f) of the constitution of the federal republic of Nigeria 1999 provides that “it shall be the duty of every citizen to declare his income honestly to the appropriate and lawful agencies and pay his tax promptly”.in addition, you are required by section 41(3) of Personal Income tax Act CAP P8 LFN2004 (as amended) to file annual returns of your income for assessment with the Ondo State Internal Revenue Service BIR and pay your tax on or before 31<sup>St</sup> of march each year. Your assessable income includes salaries from the religious organisation, income from private business and income from other sources.[/pillar_accordion_content][/pillar_accordion][vc_empty_space height=\"5rem\"][vc_text_separator title=\"Withholding Taxes\"][pillar_accordion type=\"accordion accordion--oneopen\"][pillar_accordion_content title=\" What is withholding tax?\"]Withholding tax is the specified amount deducted at source from payment accruing or made to individuals or corporate entities in respect of income receivable from service(s) rendered or from investment and remittance of same to Relevant Tax Authority in line with the provision of Personal Income Tax (PITA) and companies Income Tax Act(CITA)[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Is withholding tax another form of Tax? \"]Yes. It is another form of tax but simply an advance payment of tax, as the tax is deducted at source can be set-off against any subsequent tax liability payable on such income by the recipient (tax payer).[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"What are the services/payment on which withholding taxes must be deducted?\"]Withholding taxes must be deducted from payment due to corporate bodies and individuals on rents Commission, Management/Professional fees, Consultancy fees, Technical fees, Dividend, Directors fees, Agency Arrangement, Tenancy Agreement, Supplies.[/pillar_accordion_content][pillar_accordion_content title=\"Are there any penalties for failure to deduct and/or remit withholding tax?\"]Yes. A person or corporate body who fails to deduct or having deduct fails to remit such deduction within 30 days shall be liable to a penalty of an amount of 10% of the tax not deducted or not remitted plus interest at the prevailing monetary rate of central bank of Nigeria.[/pillar_accordion_content][/pillar_accordion][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'FAQ', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '3123-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-04-12 09:11:41', '2018-04-12 09:11:41', '', 3123, 'http://www.odbir.com/3123-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2990, 6, '2018-03-09 20:05:45', '2018-03-09 20:05:45', '[vc_row full_width=\"stretch_row\" el_class=\".hero__slide {height: 55%;}\"][vc_column][pillar_slider slider_height=\"height-70\"][pillar_slider_content image=\"2123\"]\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 30px;\">Your civic duty\r\n<strong>The key to development!!!</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\">The board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex\r\ngovernment agency charge with the responsibility\r\nof superintending internally generated revenue in Ondo state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\"><a class=\"btn\" style=\"background-color: #ff6600;\" href=\"http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/contact-us\"><span class=\"btn__text\">More Details</span></a></p>\r\n[/pillar_slider_content][pillar_slider_content image=\"2487\"]\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 30px;\">Your civic duty\r\n<strong>The key to development!!!</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\">The board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex\r\ngovernment agency charge with the responsibility\r\nof superintending internally generated revenue in Ondo state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\"><a class=\"btn\" style=\"background-color: #ff6600;\" href=\"/pages/about-company/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">More Details</span></a></p>\r\n[/pillar_slider_content][/pillar_slider][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 40px; font-weight: 300; text-align: center;\">Services that makes the process easier<em>.</em></h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Getting information for filing your taxes just got easier</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Folder-WithDocument\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Types\"]Determines the different types of tax collected by the different taxation bodies. Makes clear the outlines used by different taxation bodies for the various types of tax.[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Monitor-Analytics\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Systems\"]The Nigerian tax is lopsided and dominated majorly by oil revenue and imports, therefore the establishment of effective and efficient tax systems faces some formidable challenges. Nigeria can use its tax system as a tool.[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Financial\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Collection\"]To enable a transparent, innovative and convenience method of tax collection to help avoid multiple taxation of citizens and organizations, various methods has been introduced.\r\n\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Libra-2\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Legislation\"]The importance of taxation in any economy cannot be overemphasized, and its effects remain significant. It helps greatly in the redistribution of income and gives the government funds.\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1508801036018{padding-top: 70px !important;padding-right: 10px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 10px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center;\">Interested in taking a Self Assessment?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" style=\"border: 2px solid white;\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">CLICK HERE</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Phone-2\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Pay Tax\"]Feel free to call us on\r\nOffice: +2348033880944[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Mail-withAtSign\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Contact Us\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Feel free to email us at\r\n<b>contactus@odbir.com</b>\r\nand we will get back to you</p>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Map-Marker2\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Our Address\"]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Ondo State Board of Internal Revenue,\r\nAlagbaka, Ondo State.\r\nMonday - Friday, 8am - 7pm</p>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][pillar_text_image layout=\"boxed\" image=\"2151\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Post-Sign\" layout=\"large\" alignment=\"text-center\"]\r\n<h4 style=\"font-weight: 300;\"><a href=\"#\">Find our Tax Stations</a>\r\nAround Ondo State</h4>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/pillar_text_image][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][pillar_text_image layout=\"boxed\" image=\"2181\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Letter-Open\" layout=\"large\" alignment=\"text-center\"]\r\n<h4 style=\"font-weight: 300;\"><a href=\"#\">Interesting Updates on</a>\r\nRevenue in Ondo State</h4>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/pillar_text_image][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--white\" css=\".vc_custom_1465405568262{padding-top: 70px !important;padding-bottom: 70px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">Our Partners<em>.</em></h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Getting information for filing your taxes just got easier</span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"section--container\"></div>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner][pillar_client pppage=\"3\"][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'ODBIR Homepage', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '723-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-03-09 20:05:45', '2018-03-09 20:05:45', '', 723, 'http://www.odbir.com/723-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(2988, 6, '2018-03-09 19:37:32', '2018-03-09 19:37:32', '[vc_row full_width=\"stretch_row\" el_class=\".hero__slide {height: 55%;}\"][vc_column][pillar_slider slider_height=\"height-70\"][pillar_slider_content image=\"2123\"]\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 30px;\">Your civic duty\r\n<strong>The key to development!!!</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\">The board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex\r\ngovernment agency charge with the responsibility\r\nof superintending internally generated revenue in Ondo state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\"><a class=\"btn\" style=\"background-color: #ff6600;\" href=\"http://www.ondoweb.ondostate.gov.ng/bir/contact-us\"><span class=\"btn__text\">More Details</span></a></p>\r\n[/pillar_slider_content][pillar_slider_content image=\"2487\"]\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 30px;\">Your civic duty\r\n<strong>The key to development!!!</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\">The board of internal revenue (BIR) is the apex\r\ngovernment agency charge with the responsibility\r\nof superintending internally generated revenue in Ondo state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 18px;\"><a class=\"btn\" style=\"background-color: #ff6600;\" href=\"/pages/about-company/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">More Details</span></a></p>\r\n[/pillar_slider_content][/pillar_slider][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 40px; font-weight: 300; text-align: center;\">Services that makes the process easier<em>.</em></h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Getting information for filing your taxes just got easier</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Folder-WithDocument\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Types\"]Determines the different types of tax collected by the different taxation bodies. Makes clear the outlines used by different taxation bodies for the various types of tax.[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Monitor-Analytics\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Systems\"]The Nigerian tax is lopsided and dominated majorly by oil revenue and imports, therefore the establishment of effective and efficient tax systems faces some formidable challenges. Nigeria can use its tax system as a tool.[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Financial\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Collection\"]To enable a transparent, innovative and convenience method of tax collection to help avoid multiple taxation of citizens and organizations, various methods has been introduced.\r\n\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Libra-2\" layout=\"boxed\" title=\"Tax Legislation\"]The importance of taxation in any economy cannot be overemphasized, and its effects remain significant. It helps greatly in the redistribution of income and gives the government funds.\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--primary\" css=\".vc_custom_1508801036018{padding-top: 70px !important;padding-right: 10px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 10px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center;\">Interested in taking a Self Assessment?</h4>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn--sm\" style=\"border: 2px solid white;\" href=\"/pages/contact-map-iframe/\"><span class=\"btn__text\">CLICK HERE</span></a></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Add-Basket\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Pay Tax\"]Feel free to call us on\r\n<strong>0 (700) 225-55477</strong>\r\nMonday - Friday, 8am - 7pm[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Mail-withAtSign\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Contact Us\"]Feel free to call us on\r\n<strong>0 (700) 225-55477</strong>\r\nMonday - Friday, 8am - 7pm[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/3\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Map-Marker2\" layout=\"boxed-large\" alignment=\"text-center\" title=\"Our Address\"]Drop us a line anytime at\r\n<strong><a href=\"mailto:ondostaterevenue@gmail.com\">ondostaterevenue@gmail.com</a></strong>\r\nand we\'ll get back soon.[/pillar_icon_box][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][pillar_text_image layout=\"boxed\" image=\"2151\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Post-Sign\" layout=\"large\" alignment=\"text-center\"]\r\n<h4 style=\"font-weight: 300;\"><a href=\"#\">Find our Tax Stations</a>\r\nAround Ondo</h4>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/pillar_text_image][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][pillar_text_image layout=\"boxed\" image=\"2181\"][pillar_icon_box icon=\"icon-Letter-Open\" layout=\"large\" alignment=\"text-center\"]\r\n<h4 style=\"font-weight: 300;\"><a href=\"#\">Interesting Updates on</a>\r\nRevenue in Ondo</h4>\r\n[/pillar_icon_box][/pillar_text_image][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row el_class=\"bg--white\" css=\".vc_custom_1465405568262{padding-top: 70px !important;padding-bottom: 70px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text]\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">Our Partners<em>.</em></h3>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Getting information for filing your taxes just got easier</span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"section--container\"></div>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/4\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"3/4\"][pillar_client pppage=\"3\"][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Agency', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '723-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-03-09 19:37:32', '2018-03-09 19:37:32', '', 723, 'http://www.odbir.com/723-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
